firedamp
========

Methane plume aggregator. Maps satellite-detected methane plumes
alongside O&G infrastructure from the OGIM database, and shows a
per-plume source attribution produced offline by a research agent
(see agent/) and served from a static dataset.

Live: https://research.datadesk.eco/firedamp/


Plume sources
-------------
- Carbon Mapper      satellite + aircraft hyperspectral (API)
- IMEO / MARS        UNEP methane plume database (web scrape)
- SRON               TROPOMI weekly plume CSVs (FTP)
- OGIM v2.7          global O&G infrastructure (Zenodo GeoPackage)


Repo layout
-----------
    web/             static frontend (ES modules, no build step, no npm)
      app.js           entry point: data load, layer assembly, UI wiring
      map.js           map instance + basemap style
      plumes.js        binary parser, plume layers, filters
      ogim.js          OGIM layers, toggle, proximity queries
      detail.js        detail panel, permalinks, interactions
      analysis.js      static attribution lookup/render + wind stat
      util.js          geometry + formatting helpers
      style.css
      index.html
      vendor/          MapLibre, PMTiles, Inter font
    scripts/         Python ETL (uv-managed)
      fetch_carbon_mapper.py
      fetch_sron.py
      fetch_imeo.py
      build.py         aggregates everything into web/data/plumes.bin
      build_ogim.sh    OGIM GeoPackage -> PMTiles (slow, ~30 min)
      dist.sh          assembles the Pages artifact (cache-busted)
      serve.py         dev server with HTTP Range for PMTiles
      vendor.sh
    agent/           offline per-plume attribution agent -> attributions.json
    data/            input CSVs and intermediates (gitignored)
    .github/workflows/
      deploy.yml          Pages on push to main
      update-data.yml     plume refresh every 6 h


Setup
-----
Requires Python (managed with uv). OGIM rebuild additionally requires
ogr2ogr, tippecanoe, and tile-join.

    make vendor        download vendored JS/CSS/fonts
    make serve         dev server on :8000


Pipelines
---------
    make data          fetch CM + SRON + IMEO, build plumes.bin
    make ogim          OGIM GeoPackage -> PMTiles
    make ogim-upload   upload PMTiles to GCS
    make rebuild       full pipeline: data + ogim + upload


Source attribution
------------------
Detail panels show a per-plume source attribution served entirely from
web/data/attributions.json, produced offline by the research agent in
agent/ (pi headless + DeepSeek, per-plume local evidence + web search).
Plumes carrying an attribution render as filled discs on the map. There
is no live in-browser LLM pipeline. See agent/task.md and CLAUDE.md.


URL scheme
----------
    Map position     #map=<zoom>/<lat>/<lon>
    Plume permalink  #plume=<id>


Deployment
----------
Push to main -> deploy.yml -> GitHub Pages. plumes.bin is pulled from
the `latest-data` GitHub Release at deploy time. update-data.yml
rebuilds plumes.bin every 6 h. OGIM PMTiles are deployed separately
via `make ogim-upload` to gs://firedamp-data/.

Both workflows assemble the Pages artifact via scripts/dist.sh — add
any new web asset there.


